In particular, we see that the volume element in cylindrical coordinates is 

		dV = r dr dθ dz

(Recall that the cylindrical coordinate r is usually taken to be nonnegative. 
Given this convention, we may omit the absolute value sign in the change of variables formula)
The geometry behind this volume element is quite plauseible: A "differential box" in rΘz-space is transformed to a portion of a solid cylinder that is nearly a box itself. 
